&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">dougmit...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; Hey Ista,<br>&gt; Thanks very much for your response. I don&#39;t love the idea of having to edit<br>&gt; the raw data in order to match what I consider a formatting issue. I am not<br>&gt; sure if others have an opinion on this, but perhaps I could put this in as a<br>&gt; feature request. If I am missing a reason on why this would be a bad idea,<br>&gt; please let me know!<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Cheers,<br>&gt; Doug<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt; On Tuesday, December 18, 2012 12:44:26 PM UTC-8, izahn wrote:<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; Hi Doug,<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; I think you have to change the data, but that should be easy enough.<br>&gt;&gt; If you want to replace all the paces with newlines:<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; Dat &lt;- data.frame(x=rnorm(10),<br>&gt;&gt;                   y=rnorm(10),<br>&gt;&gt;                   Group=rep(c(&quot;This string is quite long&quot;,<br>&gt;&gt;                   &quot;This string is even longer than the other long<br>&gt;&gt; string&quot;),<br>&gt;&gt;                   each=5))<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; Dat$Group &lt;- gsub(&quot; &quot;, &quot;
&quot;, Dat$Group)<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; If you want more complicated wrapping you can use str_wrap in the<br>&gt;&gt; stringr package:<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; library(stringr)<br>&gt;&gt; Dat$Group &lt;- str_wrap(Dat$Group, width = 20)<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; Best,<br>&gt;&gt; Ista<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; On Tue, Dec 18, 2012 at 2:42 PM, Doug Mitarotonda<br>&gt;&gt; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">dougmit...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Hi,<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; I am trying to figure out the best way to add a new line (&quot;
&quot;)character<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; to<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; facet titles. The only way I can think of is going into my data and<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; adding a<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; new line in the raw data, e.g., &quot;Group 1&quot; becomes &quot;Group
1&quot; (similar to<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; suggestion in previous post:<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; <a href="https://groups.google.com/forum/?fromgroups=#!searchin/ggplot2/new$20line$20facet$20title/ggplot2/ME8rwCMy_DM/E2BUPZ8Am0wJ" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?fromgroups%3D%23!searchin/ggplot2/new$20line$20facet$20title/ggplot2/ME8rwCMy_DM/E2BUPZ8Am0wJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792373768943000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03ibrLBd-wG3tsjzHp7Ho8">https://groups.google.com/forum/?fromgroups=#!searchin/ggplot2/new$20line$20facet$20title/ggplot2/ME8rwCMy_DM/E2BUPZ8Am0wJ</a>),<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; so that when I factor the levels would match up. But I was hoping there<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; was<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; a way to just handle the titles themselves without touching the data. Is<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; that possible?<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Thanks,<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Doug<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; --<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; mailing<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; list.<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Please provide a reproducible example:<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; <a href="https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792373768943000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1V4_OPlLHVNZ8Sm-Uieojd">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>&gt;&gt; &gt; To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>&gt;&gt; &gt; More options: <a href="http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://group